+    }
+
+    // Trailing paragraphs entirely within the common suffix: same content, shifted by however
+    // much the edit changed the document's total length. Symmetric caveat to `lead`: the very
+    // first paragraph has no real delimiting `'\n'` before it (just the start of the document),
+    // so an edit at the very start can make its bytes look like a "common suffix" of themselves
+    // while actually belonging to a differently-bounded paragraph in the new text (the inserted
+    // text merges into it, with no newline of its own) -- the shifted range has to still match
+    // the new paragraph at that position, not just have content-identical bytes.
